there were many ways how Paul Beeston  influenced medical education the  activity of Morning Report gathering all  of his residence around a table usually  with coffee and tea and having them  present there the admitting diagnosis  the history and the physical examination  of each of the patients admitted to the  medical service the previous day morning  report spread from Yale to other  institutions and is still a part of  medical education of clinical practice  today his major scientific contribution  that's been described is his lifelong  study of fever on one hand he published  with Bob Peters Dorf the causes of fever  of unknown origin and on the other at a  basic science level he figured out the  cause of fever in pursuing that work  Beason was looking for the cause of  fever at the high at the level of the  hypothalamus and discovered cytokines  along with Elijah Atkins and Charles  Donatello and others working in his  group he was someone who really could  balance and show others how to balance a  devotion to patients sitting at their  bedside pursuing the diagnosis of those  patients teaching those around him in a  very humble but highly effective manner  and coupled that with investigation in  the laboratory
 

